or access the service/repair kit from the <strong>Aro Service Kits</strong> section, which combines screws, gaskets and many types of rings. Service kits come in two types: a wet kit for the wet end of your pneumatic double diaphragm pump, and a kit used for maintenance and repair of the air side of your air-operated double diaphragm pump. Since these two kits contain different products, you should make your choice by considering which products you need and where you will use them.</p><p>If you want to purchase products individually outside the <strong>Aro Service Kits</strong>, you can also access <strong>Aro gaskets, Aro rings, Aro valve balls, Aro valve seats, Aro hardware and Aro diaphragms</strong>. However, keep in mind that the application area in which each industry uses its pumps, and the appropriate Aro spare part for that area, will vary. Based on your specific application needs such as chemical compatibility, temperature and sealing capacity, HD Marine offers its customers high-quality, widely used and preferred materials and products such as <strong>Santoprene, Hytrel, N-fit, PTFE and Neoprene</strong> in pump parts.</p></div> </div>$h$, NULL, $h$Electric Sump Oil Extraction Pump 80 L – 6980 | HD Marine$h$, $h$Aro® first introduced its air-operated double diaphragm pump in the eighties in Bryan, Ohio (United States). Today, ARO® is part of Ingersoll Rand Corp…$h$, 'auto') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
